":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0064"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bd18ebf05dedcfe1f8bdc3b2684907dfd28bad4c4f7460ece446bec2bccbe86d","title":"When do Kähler-potential derivative interactions permit modulus decay into stringy axions or Nambu–Goldstone bosons without final-state mass suppression, and what does this imply for reheating, dark radiation and axino dark matter?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0067"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bdcada247c2c32effba113dc0702b4aba591190d913f74a5bab9da2fb7056bd3","title":"Can the conjectured instability of cold, near-extremal planar AdS black holes impose a lower bound on the enthalpy density of holographically modelled cold strongly coupled matter?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bdc8ddf7099a72b2173d5f4641bc755cf098b17ba56f1146d4f9b2bea80d7a9e","title":"How large can charges of massless or light fields become under a U(1) in four-dimensional F-theory, particularly a U(1) decoupled from other gauge sectors? The paper constructs large-charge examples and asks whether their charges approach a landscape upper bound.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0078"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bdf51ca695d22b33b50e6af0fec0217123da1a933a3a484d9e6f53af50d2edc7","title":"How can tension-dependent BCFT2 thermodynamics be combined with the effective JT thermodynamics seen by EOW-brane observers, and what do these observers see when temperature is lowered and the branes meet?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0084"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:bd5d0c80906c091a30ec6517bf3da47510f1fa0ce60962bc236bb6a79f2f09a5","title":"Does a universal asymptotic relation connect the leading light tower’s mass variation to the specie